<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n284" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăcācĭa</span></b> ,
		ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκακία</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The acacia-tree</i>, <i>the Egyptian
				pod-thorn</i>: Mimosa Nilotica, Linn.; described by <i><span class="en">Plin.
				24, 12, 67, § 109 sq.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The juice</i> or <i>gum</i> of the
			same, <i><span class="en">Cels.
				6, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 20, 21, 85, § 233</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 23 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
